course: dictionary
lesson: 2330
title: Words from stories and history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to stories, history or belief, and you may meet them in a religious lesson, a history book or a museum. Context still helps you find their meaning. «On the third day after the crucifixion some women went to Jesus' tomb and found the stone rolled away and the tomb empty.» The clues are the third day, the tomb and the empty stone, which tell you that something very important happened before that day.
explain: Crucifixion is a noun, a word for a naming thing. It means being killed by being fixed to a cross. When you see a capital C, as in the Crucifixion, it names one special event: the death of Jesus on the cross, which Christians remember on Good Friday.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «After the death of Jesus on the cross, some women went to his tomb» still makes sense, so your meaning fits. Always ask: does my meaning make the whole sentence clear?
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. In history, crucifixion names a cruel punishment used by the Romans long ago. In art, it can name a painting or statue showing Jesus on the cross. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: Crucifixion means being put to death by being fixed to a cross.
fact: «The Crucifixion» with a capital C means the death of Jesus on the cross.
fact: Christians remember the Crucifixion on Good Friday, just before Easter.
fact: The Romans used crucifixion as a cruel punishment long ago.
fact: A crucifixion can also be a painting or statue showing Jesus on the cross.
exercise: «On the third day after the crucifixion some women went to Jesus' tomb.» What does crucifixion mean here? | A big festival in the city | A school trip to a museum | A long journey across a desert | *The death of Jesus on a cross
exercise: Which day do Christians remember the Crucifixion? | Boxing Day | Christmas Day | Bonfire Night | *Good Friday
exercise: In history lessons, what was crucifixion used for? | A school rule about homework | *A cruel punishment | A way to plant seeds | A kind way of giving a gift
test: What is a crucifixion in a painting? | A picture of a ship at sea | A map of Jerusalem | A picture of the sun rising | *A painting or statue showing Jesus on the cross
test: What is a tomb? | A school bag | A kind of small boat | *A place where a dead body is laid | A type of tall tree
exam: Which is the best way to check the meaning of crucifixion in a new sentence? | Ignore the word and guess the whole sentence | Look only at the first letter of the word | Stop reading the text completely | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
